  name: Exhaust Gas Analyser
  description: "An exhaust gas analyzer is a device used to measure the level of
    pollutants emitted from a vehicle\u2019s exhaust system. It detects gases such
    as carbon monoxide (CO), carbon dioxide (CO\u2082), hydrocarbons (HC), and nitrogen
    oxides (NOx). This tool is essential for emissions testing, environmental compliance,
    and diagnosing engine combustion efficiency."
